course: dictionary
lesson: 11069
title: Weight and lifter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A weightlifter is a person who lifts heavy weights, often a long metal bar with discs on each end, as a sport or to get stronger. Break the word into two parts: weight and lifter. A lifter is someone who lifts, so a weightlifter is someone who lifts weights.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «An Olympic weightlifter» tells you the sport is at the Olympic Games, and «a strong weightlifter» tells you the person has great strength. Ask yourself what would fit in the gap, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: In the giraffe sentence, «just as a weightlifter's babies are not born with big muscles» shows that the muscles a weightlifter builds by training are not passed on to their children. Context can show you what a word is not as well as what it is.
fact: A weightlifter is a person who lifts heavy weights, especially a barbell, as a sport or to get stronger.
fact: Weightlifting is an Olympic sport with two lifts: the snatch and the clean and jerk.
fact: In maths, you add up the weight of the bar and the discs on each side to find the total weight lifted.
fact: Weightlifters train with a coach so they can lift safely.
fact: «Stretching your body does not change the DNA you pass on»; a weightlifter's babies are not born with big muscles.
exercise: What is a weightlifter? | A person who sells weights in a shop | A runner who races around a track | *A person who lifts heavy weights as a sport or to get stronger | A person who weighs parcels at the post office
exercise: A bar weighs 20 kg. You add one 10 kg disc on each side. What is the total weight? | 30 kg | 60 kg | 20 kg | *40 kg
exercise: Which word in «an Olympic weightlifter» tells you the sport is at the Olympic Games? | *Olympic | an | weightlifter
test: Why do weightlifters train with a coach? | To win every race they enter | *To lift heavy weights safely | To eat more sweets
test: «A weightlifter's babies are not born with big muscles.» What does this sentence teach you? | Lifting weights makes babies heavier | Babies are born with big muscles | Weightlifters have no babies | *Muscles built by lifting weights are not passed on to babies
exam: Priya says a weightlifter is a runner. What is a weightlifter really? | A shop worker | A swimmer | *A person who lifts heavy weights | A person who weighs parcels
